1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,484
Sweetheart, my best friend Agnes saved for

2
00:00:03,484 --> 00:00:06,139
eleven years to fly first class,

3
00:00:06,139 --> 00:00:07,964
just once in her life.

4
00:00:08,144 --> 00:00:10,856
Christmas of two thousand twenty-three,

5
00:00:10,856 --> 00:00:12,316
she was seventy-nine,

6
00:00:12,316 --> 00:00:14,471
and she finally had the ticket.

7
00:00:14,651 --> 00:00:15,952
Seat two A.

8
00:00:16,132 --> 00:00:18,195
And ten minutes before takeoff,

9
00:00:18,195 --> 00:00:20,459
a flight attendant told her to get

10
00:00:20,459 --> 00:00:22,523
her things and move to the back

11
00:00:22,523 --> 00:00:23,388
of the plane,

12
00:00:23,388 --> 00:00:26,317
so a businessman's girlfriend could have her

13
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:26,650
seat.

14
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:28,469
What happened next,

15
00:00:28,469 --> 00:00:30,453
I saw with my own eyes.

16
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:32,956
Tonight I'm going to tell you who

17
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:34,718
walked out of that cockpit,

18
00:00:34,718 --> 00:00:37,133
what he said into the microphone that

19
00:00:37,133 --> 00:00:39,156
made a whole airplane go quiet,

20
00:00:39,156 --> 00:00:42,157
and why that businessman wouldn't look anybody

21
00:00:42,157 --> 00:00:43,854
in the eye for the rest of

22
00:00:43,854 --> 00:00:44,572
the flight.

23
00:00:44,752 --> 00:00:45,789
Stay with me,

24
00:00:45,789 --> 00:00:48,343
honey, because it goes back to a

25
00:00:48,343 --> 00:00:52,333
foster home in Mansfield in nineteen seventy-nine.

26
00:00:52,683 --> 00:00:55,766
Agnes and I have been friends since

27
00:00:55,766 --> 00:00:57,263
the second grade,

28
00:00:57,263 --> 00:00:57,792
honey.

29
00:00:57,972 --> 00:01:00,037
She married a mailman named Bill,

30
00:01:00,037 --> 00:01:02,540
and they couldn't have children of their

31
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:02,790
own.

32
00:01:02,970 --> 00:01:05,402
So in nineteen sixty-eight,

33
00:01:05,402 --> 00:01:07,835
they became foster parents.

34
00:01:08,015 --> 00:01:10,393
And over the next twenty-five years,

35
00:01:10,393 --> 00:01:12,508
they took in forty-one children.

36
00:01:12,688 --> 00:01:13,686
Forty-one.

37
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:15,346
Some stayed a week,

38
00:01:15,346 --> 00:01:17,059
some stayed ten years.

39
00:01:17,239 --> 00:01:20,051
Agnes kept a photograph of every single

40
00:01:20,051 --> 00:01:21,782
one on her refrigerator,

41
00:01:21,782 --> 00:01:24,306
and she knew all their birthdays by

42
00:01:24,306 --> 00:01:24,739
heart.

43
00:01:25,088 --> 00:01:27,030
They never had much money,

44
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:27,852
sweetheart.

45
00:01:28,032 --> 00:01:31,439
Bill's mailman salary and whatever the county

46
00:01:31,439 --> 00:01:33,256
paid, which wasn't much.

47
00:01:33,436 --> 00:01:36,175
Agnes made the children's clothes and cut

48
00:01:36,175 --> 00:01:38,312
their hair at the kitchen table.

49
00:01:38,492 --> 00:01:40,901
They never took a vacation in their

50
00:01:40,901 --> 00:01:41,314
lives.

51
00:01:41,494 --> 00:01:44,059
Bill passed in two thousand twelve.

52
00:01:44,239 --> 00:01:46,832
And Agnes had a little dream she

53
00:01:46,832 --> 00:01:47,885
told only me.

54
00:01:48,065 --> 00:01:50,375
Just once, before she died,

55
00:01:50,375 --> 00:01:52,941
she wanted to fly first class.

56
00:01:53,121 --> 00:01:55,592
With the warm nuts and the real

57
00:01:55,592 --> 00:01:56,070
glass.

58
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:58,972
Her younger sister lived in Florida,

59
00:01:58,972 --> 00:02:02,021
and they hadn't spent Christmas together in

60
00:02:02,021 --> 00:02:03,014
fifteen years.

61
00:02:03,194 --> 00:02:06,079
So Agnes started putting twenty dollars a

62
00:02:06,079 --> 00:02:07,768
month into a coffee can.

63
00:02:07,948 --> 00:02:09,400
Eleven years.

64
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:12,261
And in October of twenty twenty-three,

65
00:02:12,261 --> 00:02:15,577
she bought one first-class ticket from Columbus

66
00:02:15,577 --> 00:02:18,682
to Tampa, for the twenty-second of December.

67
00:02:18,862 --> 00:02:20,053
I went with her,

68
00:02:20,053 --> 00:02:21,691
but I sat in the back,

69
00:02:21,691 --> 00:02:24,298
in coach, because I wasn't going to

70
00:02:24,298 --> 00:02:25,340
pay that much.

71
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:27,726
In a minute I'll tell you what

72
00:02:27,726 --> 00:02:28,388
she wore.

73
00:02:28,738 --> 00:02:30,798
She wore her best red wool suit

74
00:02:30,798 --> 00:02:32,926
and the gold cross Bill gave her

75
00:02:32,926 --> 00:02:34,322
on their wedding day.

76
00:02:34,502 --> 00:02:36,718
She had her hair done the day

77
00:02:36,718 --> 00:02:37,253
before.

78
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:40,070
When they called first class to board,

79
00:02:40,070 --> 00:02:42,220
she squeezed my hand so hard it

80
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:44,579
hurt, and she walked down that jet

81
00:02:44,579 --> 00:02:45,967
bridge like a queen.

82
00:02:46,147 --> 00:02:48,140
I watched her sit down in seat

83
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:50,199
two A from the line behind her.

84
00:02:50,379 --> 00:02:52,294
She ran her hand over the leather

85
00:02:52,294 --> 00:02:53,629
like it was a fur coat.

86
00:02:53,979 --> 00:02:55,914
I was in row twenty-eight,

87
00:02:55,914 --> 00:02:57,997
sweetheart, by the bathroom.

88
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:00,866
And about ten minutes before the doors

89
00:03:00,866 --> 00:03:03,627
closed, I saw a flight attendant coming

90
00:03:03,627 --> 00:03:06,246
down the aisle with Agnes behind her,

91
00:03:06,246 --> 00:03:08,724
carrying her coat and her purse and

92
00:03:08,724 --> 00:03:11,697
her little Christmas bag with the presents

93
00:03:11,697 --> 00:03:12,759
for her sister.

94
00:03:12,939 --> 00:03:14,576
Her face was red.

95
00:03:14,756 --> 00:03:18,187
The flight attendant stopped at the empty

96
00:03:18,187 --> 00:03:19,526
seat next to me,

97
00:03:19,526 --> 00:03:22,037
row twenty-eight, middle seat,

98
00:03:22,037 --> 00:03:23,878
and said, here you go,

99
00:03:23,878 --> 00:03:24,380
ma'am.

100
00:03:24,731 --> 00:03:27,575
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

101
00:03:27,575 --> 00:03:29,769
tap the like button for me,

102
00:03:29,769 --> 00:03:30,663
sweetheart.

103
00:03:30,843 --> 00:03:34,187
It helps more people find these stories.

104
00:03:34,367 --> 00:03:37,246
I said, what in the world happened?

105
00:03:37,426 --> 00:03:39,087
And Agnes whispered,

106
00:03:39,087 --> 00:03:41,745
there's a man up front who flies

107
00:03:41,745 --> 00:03:42,825
all the time.

108
00:03:43,005 --> 00:03:45,318
He wanted his lady friend to sit

109
00:03:45,318 --> 00:03:46,186
next to him.

110
00:03:46,366 --> 00:03:48,421
They said they had to reseat me.

111
00:03:48,601 --> 00:03:50,656
They said I'd get a voucher.

112
00:03:50,836 --> 00:03:52,901
And then my best friend,

113
00:03:52,901 --> 00:03:54,879
seventy-nine years old,

114
00:03:54,879 --> 00:03:56,256
in her red suit,

115
00:03:56,256 --> 00:03:57,546
started to cry.

116
00:03:57,897 --> 00:04:00,024
I could see him from where I

117
00:04:00,024 --> 00:04:01,240
stood up, honey.

118
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:02,718
A man about fifty,

119
00:04:02,718 --> 00:04:05,097
in a vest with the airline's logo

120
00:04:05,097 --> 00:04:07,115
on it, the kind they give to

121
00:04:07,115 --> 00:04:08,990
people who fly every week.

122
00:04:09,170 --> 00:04:12,066
A young woman with big sunglasses was

123
00:04:12,066 --> 00:04:14,023
settling into seat two A,

124
00:04:14,023 --> 00:04:15,432
into Agnes's seat,

125
00:04:15,432 --> 00:04:16,449
and laughing.

126
00:04:16,629 --> 00:04:18,954
And he said something to the flight

127
00:04:18,954 --> 00:04:21,146
attendant, and they both laughed.

128
00:04:21,326 --> 00:04:23,671
I've never wanted to march up an

129
00:04:23,671 --> 00:04:26,237
airplane aisle so badly in my life.

130
00:04:26,587 --> 00:04:27,978
I said, Agnes,

131
00:04:27,978 --> 00:04:29,768
that is not right.

132
00:04:29,948 --> 00:04:31,596
You paid for that seat.

133
00:04:31,776 --> 00:04:34,005
You saved for eleven years.

134
00:04:34,185 --> 00:04:35,834
I'm going up there.

135
00:04:36,014 --> 00:04:39,916
And Agnes grabbed my arm and said,

136
00:04:39,916 --> 00:04:40,948
Ruth, no.

137
00:04:41,128 --> 00:04:41,976
Please.

138
00:04:42,156 --> 00:04:43,677
Don't make a scene.

139
00:04:43,857 --> 00:04:46,980
I don't want to ruin anybody's Christmas.

140
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,917
And that was Agnes,

141
00:04:48,917 --> 00:04:49,935
sweetheart.

142
00:04:50,115 --> 00:04:52,911
Forty-one children, and she didn't want to

143
00:04:52,911 --> 00:04:54,642
be any trouble to anybody.

144
00:04:54,822 --> 00:04:56,309
So I sat down.

145
00:04:56,489 --> 00:04:58,056
And I was boiling.

146
00:04:58,406 --> 00:05:01,431
The flight attendant brought Agnes a little

147
00:05:01,431 --> 00:05:03,822
plastic cup of water and a voucher

148
00:05:03,822 --> 00:05:05,089
for fifty dollars,

149
00:05:05,089 --> 00:05:05,511
honey.

150
00:05:05,691 --> 00:05:07,084
Fifty dollars.

151
00:05:07,264 --> 00:05:09,749
For eleven years of coffee-can money.

152
00:05:09,929 --> 00:05:11,922
Agnes folded it up and put it

153
00:05:11,922 --> 00:05:14,329
in her purse without looking at it.

154
00:05:14,509 --> 00:05:15,815
And she said,

155
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:17,423
it's fine, Ruth.

156
00:05:17,603 --> 00:05:19,281
At least I got to sit in

157
00:05:19,281 --> 00:05:20,610
it for ten minutes.

158
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:22,798
I'll remember how it felt.

159
00:05:22,978 --> 00:05:24,847
I'll tell you what I wanted to

160
00:05:24,847 --> 00:05:26,903
do with that voucher in a minute.

161
00:05:27,253 --> 00:05:29,232
So far, the coffee can,

162
00:05:29,232 --> 00:05:30,351
the red suit,

163
00:05:30,351 --> 00:05:33,793
the businessman, and Agnes in the middle

164
00:05:33,793 --> 00:05:35,600
seat by the bathroom.

165
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:38,110
And just before the doors closed,

166
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,804
the cockpit door opened,

167
00:05:39,804 --> 00:05:42,274
and the captain stepped out to talk

168
00:05:42,274 --> 00:05:44,604
to the flight attendant up front.

169
00:05:44,784 --> 00:05:46,053
A tall Black man,

170
00:05:46,053 --> 00:05:48,817
about fifty, with gray at his temples

171
00:05:48,817 --> 00:05:51,506
and four gold stripes on his sleeve.

172
00:05:51,686 --> 00:05:53,741
He glanced down the aisle.

173
00:05:53,921 --> 00:05:55,662
Then he looked again.

174
00:05:55,842 --> 00:05:56,899
Stay with me.

175
00:05:57,249 --> 00:05:59,849
He came walking down that aisle,

176
00:05:59,849 --> 00:06:01,800
honey, all the way back,

177
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,181
past first class,

178
00:06:03,181 --> 00:06:06,188
past business, past all those rows of

179
00:06:06,188 --> 00:06:08,708
people with their seatbelts on,

180
00:06:08,708 --> 00:06:09,927
staring at him.

181
00:06:10,107 --> 00:06:12,545
And he stopped at row twenty-eight.

182
00:06:12,725 --> 00:06:15,592
And he bent down and looked at

183
00:06:15,592 --> 00:06:17,408
Agnes, and he said,

184
00:06:17,408 --> 00:06:19,702
very softly, Mama Agnes?

185
00:06:19,882 --> 00:06:21,947
And Agnes looked up at him,

186
00:06:21,947 --> 00:06:23,324
with her wet eyes,

187
00:06:23,324 --> 00:06:25,542
and she put her hand over her

188
00:06:25,542 --> 00:06:26,001
mouth.

189
00:06:26,181 --> 00:06:27,911
She said, Marcus?

190
00:06:28,261 --> 00:06:31,143
Marcus came to Agnes and Bill's house

191
00:06:31,143 --> 00:06:33,091
in nineteen seventy-nine,

192
00:06:33,091 --> 00:06:35,194
when he was nine years old,

193
00:06:35,194 --> 00:06:36,051
sweetheart.

194
00:06:36,231 --> 00:06:38,982
He'd been in six homes already.

195
00:06:39,162 --> 00:06:41,550
He didn't talk for the first three

196
00:06:41,550 --> 00:06:42,042
months.

197
00:06:42,222 --> 00:06:43,557
Not one word.

198
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:45,819
He just sat at the window and

199
00:06:45,819 --> 00:06:48,835
watched the airplanes from the airfield go

200
00:06:48,835 --> 00:06:49,194
over.

201
00:06:49,374 --> 00:06:50,409
And one night,

202
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:52,702
Bill sat down beside him with a

203
00:06:52,702 --> 00:06:56,253
library book about airplanes and started reading

204
00:06:56,253 --> 00:06:57,141
it out loud.

205
00:06:57,321 --> 00:07:00,026
Marcus said his first word that night.

206
00:07:00,206 --> 00:07:01,181
Bill.

207
00:07:01,531 --> 00:07:03,878
Bill took him to the airfield every

208
00:07:03,878 --> 00:07:05,220
Saturday after that,

209
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:07,568
to watch the small planes take off.

210
00:07:07,748 --> 00:07:10,262
Agnes sewed him a pilot's cap out

211
00:07:10,262 --> 00:07:11,939
of an old blue blazer.

212
00:07:12,119 --> 00:07:14,742
He stayed with them for nine years,

213
00:07:14,742 --> 00:07:17,065
until he graduated high school.

214
00:07:17,245 --> 00:07:19,160
He went into the Air Force.

215
00:07:19,340 --> 00:07:20,972
And they lost touch,

216
00:07:20,972 --> 00:07:22,197
the way you do.

217
00:07:22,377 --> 00:07:25,548
Agnes had his picture on her refrigerator

218
00:07:25,548 --> 00:07:26,786
for forty years,

219
00:07:26,786 --> 00:07:28,797
in that homemade blue cap.

220
00:07:28,977 --> 00:07:31,043
In a minute I'll tell you what

221
00:07:31,043 --> 00:07:32,077
he said to her.

222
00:07:32,427 --> 00:07:34,465
He said, Mama Agnes,

223
00:07:34,465 --> 00:07:37,523
why are you sitting back here?

224
00:07:37,703 --> 00:07:40,142
And Agnes tried to say it was

225
00:07:40,142 --> 00:07:40,815
nothing.

226
00:07:40,995 --> 00:07:42,815
But I'm not Agnes,

227
00:07:42,815 --> 00:07:43,421
honey.

228
00:07:43,601 --> 00:07:44,983
I told him.

229
00:07:45,163 --> 00:07:46,010
All of it.

230
00:07:46,190 --> 00:07:47,528
The coffee can,

231
00:07:47,528 --> 00:07:49,045
the eleven years,

232
00:07:49,045 --> 00:07:50,026
seat two A,

233
00:07:50,026 --> 00:07:51,810
the man in the vest.

234
00:07:51,990 --> 00:07:54,915
And I watched that captain's face go

235
00:07:54,915 --> 00:07:55,809
very still.

236
00:07:55,989 --> 00:07:57,046
He stood up.

237
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:59,525
He said, excuse me,

238
00:07:59,525 --> 00:08:00,372
ladies.

239
00:08:00,552 --> 00:08:02,622
And he walked back up the aisle

240
00:08:02,622 --> 00:08:03,489
to the front.

241
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,193
I found out later,

242
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:08,126
honey, that Marcus had looked for Agnes

243
00:08:08,126 --> 00:08:08,878
for years.

244
00:08:09,058 --> 00:08:11,032
When he got his wings in the

245
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:13,146
Air Force, he wrote to the old

246
00:08:13,146 --> 00:08:14,908
house on Sycamore Street,

247
00:08:14,908 --> 00:08:16,952
but by then Agnes had sold it

248
00:08:16,952 --> 00:08:19,559
and moved to a little apartment after

249
00:08:19,559 --> 00:08:22,096
Bill died, and the letter came back.

250
00:08:22,276 --> 00:08:24,831
He didn't know Bill had passed.

251
00:08:25,011 --> 00:08:27,624
He'd been flying over Ohio for thirty

252
00:08:27,624 --> 00:08:30,520
years, looking down and wondering if they

253
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:31,721
were still there.

254
00:08:32,071 --> 00:08:33,158
A minute later,

255
00:08:33,158 --> 00:08:34,753
the speakers crackled.

256
00:08:34,933 --> 00:08:37,569
And his voice came over the whole

257
00:08:37,569 --> 00:08:38,288
airplane.

258
00:08:38,468 --> 00:08:40,790
He said, ladies and gentlemen,

259
00:08:40,790 --> 00:08:42,415
this is your captain.

260
00:08:42,595 --> 00:08:43,881
Before we leave,

261
00:08:43,881 --> 00:08:45,971
I want to tell you about a

262
00:08:45,971 --> 00:08:46,775
passenger.

263
00:08:46,955 --> 00:08:48,746
In nineteen seventy-nine,

264
00:08:48,746 --> 00:08:51,111
I was a little boy nobody wanted.

265
00:08:51,291 --> 00:08:53,915
I'd been in six foster homes.

266
00:08:54,095 --> 00:08:56,287
And a mailman and his wife took

267
00:08:56,287 --> 00:08:58,266
me in, and they taught me to

268
00:08:58,266 --> 00:09:00,528
read, and they taught me to love

269
00:09:00,528 --> 00:09:01,235
airplanes.

270
00:09:01,585 --> 00:09:04,623
He said, that woman raised forty-one children

271
00:09:04,623 --> 00:09:05,973
who weren't her own.

272
00:09:06,153 --> 00:09:08,758
She saved for eleven years for seat

273
00:09:08,758 --> 00:09:10,321
two A on this flight.

274
00:09:10,501 --> 00:09:12,211
And a few minutes ago,

275
00:09:12,211 --> 00:09:14,387
she was moved to the back of

276
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,319
my airplane.

277
00:09:15,499 --> 00:09:16,467
Then he said,

278
00:09:16,467 --> 00:09:18,924
I'm the captain of this aircraft.

279
00:09:19,104 --> 00:09:20,381
And Mrs.

280
00:09:20,561 --> 00:09:23,512
Agnes Hoyt will be sitting in seat

281
00:09:23,512 --> 00:09:24,033
two A.

282
00:09:24,213 --> 00:09:25,919
There was a silence,

283
00:09:25,919 --> 00:09:26,430
honey.

284
00:09:26,610 --> 00:09:29,060
And then somebody started clapping.

285
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:32,038
And then the whole airplane was clapping.

286
00:09:32,388 --> 00:09:35,350
The flight attendant came back to row

287
00:09:35,350 --> 00:09:38,312
twenty-eight, with her face as red as

288
00:09:38,312 --> 00:09:40,473
Agnes's suit, and she said,

289
00:09:40,473 --> 00:09:40,793
Mrs.

290
00:09:40,973 --> 00:09:42,814
Hoyt, I am so sorry,

291
00:09:42,814 --> 00:09:44,746
please, come with me.

292
00:09:44,926 --> 00:09:47,713
And Agnes walked back up that aisle,

293
00:09:47,713 --> 00:09:50,035
honey, with her Christmas bag,

294
00:09:50,035 --> 00:09:52,899
and people were reaching out to touch

295
00:09:52,899 --> 00:09:53,518
her arm.

296
00:09:53,698 --> 00:09:56,078
A sailor in uniform stood up.

297
00:09:56,258 --> 00:09:58,255
An old man saluted.

298
00:09:58,435 --> 00:10:01,160
Agnes was crying so hard she couldn't

299
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,928
see where she was going.

300
00:10:03,278 --> 00:10:05,962
The young woman in the sunglasses had

301
00:10:05,962 --> 00:10:08,502
already moved, without being asked.

302
00:10:08,682 --> 00:10:11,460
She went back to row twenty-eight and

303
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:13,037
sat right next to me,

304
00:10:13,037 --> 00:10:14,013
and she said,

305
00:10:14,013 --> 00:10:15,665
quietly, I'm so sorry,

306
00:10:15,665 --> 00:10:16,716
I didn't know.

307
00:10:16,896 --> 00:10:18,649
And I'll give her credit.

308
00:10:18,829 --> 00:10:19,805
She meant it.

309
00:10:19,985 --> 00:10:21,559
But the man in the vest,

310
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:24,250
sweetheart, didn't look up from his phone

311
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:26,022
for the rest of the flight.

312
00:10:26,202 --> 00:10:27,374
Not once.

313
00:10:27,554 --> 00:10:29,845
Two hours and twenty minutes,

314
00:10:29,845 --> 00:10:31,583
staring at that phone.

315
00:10:31,933 --> 00:10:33,841
When we landed in Tampa,

316
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:36,465
Marcus asked Agnes to stay on the

317
00:10:36,465 --> 00:10:38,771
plane until everyone was off.

318
00:10:38,951 --> 00:10:41,069
Then he took her into the cockpit

319
00:10:41,069 --> 00:10:43,123
and let her sit in the captain's

320
00:10:43,123 --> 00:10:43,444
seat.

321
00:10:43,624 --> 00:10:46,404
And he reached into his flight bag,

322
00:10:46,404 --> 00:10:49,342
honey, and pulled out a little folded

323
00:10:49,342 --> 00:10:51,010
square of blue cloth,

324
00:10:51,010 --> 00:10:52,599
faded and worn soft.

325
00:10:52,779 --> 00:10:54,172
It was the cap.

326
00:10:54,352 --> 00:10:57,756
The homemade pilot's cap Agnes sewed from

327
00:10:57,756 --> 00:10:59,251
Bill's old blazer.

328
00:10:59,431 --> 00:11:02,174
He'd carried it on every single flight

329
00:11:02,174 --> 00:11:03,402
for thirty years.

330
00:11:03,752 --> 00:11:06,760
Marcus spent Christmas Day with Agnes and

331
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:08,447
her sister, sweetheart,

332
00:11:08,447 --> 00:11:10,942
and his wife and his two daughters

333
00:11:10,942 --> 00:11:12,703
drove over from Orlando.

334
00:11:12,883 --> 00:11:14,923
And now every Christmas,

335
00:11:14,923 --> 00:11:17,643
he flies Agnes to Tampa himself.

336
00:11:17,823 --> 00:11:20,261
First class, seat two A.

337
00:11:20,441 --> 00:11:21,788
She's eighty-two now.

338
00:11:21,968 --> 00:11:23,558
And the man in the vest?

339
00:11:23,738 --> 00:11:26,338
Agnes got a letter from the airline

340
00:11:26,338 --> 00:11:28,938
in January, with an apology and two

341
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:29,903
free tickets.

342
00:11:30,083 --> 00:11:32,133
She gave them both to a young

343
00:11:32,133 --> 00:11:34,112
foster mother at her church.

344
00:11:34,462 --> 00:11:37,118
Here's what I want you to remember,

345
00:11:37,118 --> 00:11:37,573
honey.

346
00:11:37,753 --> 00:11:40,288
You never know who that old woman

347
00:11:40,288 --> 00:11:42,439
in the back of the line used

348
00:11:42,439 --> 00:11:44,359
to be, or who she raised.

349
00:11:44,539 --> 00:11:46,438
Treat her like she matters,

350
00:11:46,438 --> 00:11:47,845
because to somebody,

351
00:11:47,845 --> 00:11:49,392
she's the whole world.

352
00:11:49,572 --> 00:11:51,340
Tell me in the comments,

353
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:54,507
sweetheart, is there someone who raised you

354
00:11:54,507 --> 00:11:56,201
who wasn't your family?

355
00:11:56,381 --> 00:11:58,665
There are more of my family's stories

356
00:11:58,665 --> 00:12:00,826
in the playlist right there on your

357
00:12:00,826 --> 00:12:01,258
screen.

358
00:12:01,438 --> 00:12:02,483
Good night.

359
00:12:02,663 --> 00:12:04,102
Merry Christmas.
